Prior objects on this same mechanism, in order:

efl_absorption_method (v1): reserve described as completed by sequential,
iterative coloring. Closed T, banked clean, but grounding FAILED Axiom C
(chose self-referential topology with non-holographic dimensionality, which
the axiom forbids).

efl_absorption_method_v2: reserve described as fully pre-determined in
advance. Grounded clean this time, but the word's own bank check came back
vacuous, no live clears, nothing deposited. Making the outcome fully known
ahead of time removed the fork's real content.

efl_absorption_method_v3: reserve described as built with redundant
flexibility for whichever specific leftover pattern occurs, kept as a live
uncertainty. Grounded clean AND banked clean and non-vacuous, both
properties held at once for the first time.

efl_absorption_resolution: the same mechanism closed into its actual
completed outcome. Also clean and non-vacuous.

Both v3 and the resolution ground to the same distinguishing signature,
checked by machine-diffing their own grounded tuples against the
affirmation's and negation's tuples position by position (same instrument,
not compared across codecs): topology reads irreducible, symmetry reads as
quantum superposition, criticality lands exactly on the self-referential
fixed point, and multiplicity reads n:m rather than the n:n both the
affirmation and negation carry on that axis. Read together: a dialetheic
object that holds every possible leftover pattern against one completed
reserve without needing to resolve which specific pattern occurs first.

This object is the next step down from that reading: not the mechanism, not
its resolved outcome, but the totality claim underneath both of them, that
the reserve's n:m relation actually covers every leftover pattern the greedy
phase could produce, with none left unmatched. That totality is what an
actual Lean proof of the reserve step would need to establish.
